      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "The Investment",
        "title": "Studio costs add up. The FLEX AIR pays for itself fast.",
        "text": "At $650 AUD, the FLEX AIR represents extraordinary value. If you attend reformer Pilates twice a week, the FLEX AIR pays for itself within two months. After that, every session is essentially free — train as often as you like, on your own schedule, without booking, commuting, or waiting for a class."
      }
    },
    "sp_reviews": {
      "type": "sensol-reviews",
      "blocks": {
        "review_1": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "text": "I'd been wanting to try reformer Pilates for over a year but couldn't justify the studio prices — $45 a class adds up fast. The FLEX AIR cost me less than three months of studio sessions, and I can use it every day. The springs feel smooth and forgiving, which was perfect as a complete beginner. The Vesta app walked me through my first session step by step. After six weeks, I've already noticed improvements in my posture and core strength.",
            "name": "Sarah M.",
            "role": "Melbourne"
          }
        },
        "review_2": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "text": "My physio recommended reformer Pilates after my knee surgery, but the waiting list for classes was 8 weeks and private sessions were $120 each. The FLEX AIR let me start my rehabilitation at home, at my own pace. The spring resistance is gentle enough for post-surgical recovery but progressive enough that I'm still using it months later. The app's rehab programme is excellent — clear, safe, and well-structured.",
            "name": "Margaret T.",
            "role": "Brisbane"
          }
        },
        "review_3": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "text": "I compared every reformer on the Australian market before buying. The Fortis was cheaper but felt flimsy and had no app. The Your Reformer was beautiful but $2,800. The FLEX AIR hits the sweet spot: built like a proper machine, the app is genuinely useful, and it doubles as a strength trainer. I've saved hundreds compared to my old studio membership, and I workout more often because it's right there in my living room. The Lifetime Warranty sealed the deal for me.",
            "name": "Priya K.",
            "role": "Adelaide"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "review_1",
        "review_2",
        "review_3"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "show_section": true,
        "label": "Verified Owners",
        "title": "Loved by first-time reformer users."
      }
    },
    "sp_qa": {
      "type": "sensol-product-qa",
      "blocks": {
        "qa_1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the FLEX AIR suitable for complete beginners?",
            "answer": "Absolutely. The FLEX AIR was designed with beginners as the primary audience. The spring resistance provides smooth, gentle tension that's far less intimidating than springs. The Vesta Sensol App includes a dedicated 'First Time Reformer' programme that guides you through every movement with clear video and audio instructions. You can start at the lowest resistance setting and progress at your own pace."
          }
        },
        "qa_2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does spring resistance compare to springs?",
            "answer": "Springs deliver smoother, more consistent tension throughout the entire range of motion, whereas springs can feel jerky and provide uneven resistance. For beginners and rehabilitation users, this smoothness reduces the risk of strain and makes it easier to maintain proper form. Springs are also quieter, lighter, and don't suffer from the spring fatigue that degrades traditional reformers over time."
          }
        },
        "qa_3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will the FLEX AIR fit in my apartment?",
            "answer": "Almost certainly. The FLEX AIR is the only Sensol model with a foldable frame, collapsing from 185 cm to 165 cm in length. It stores upright in just 0.2 m² — about the footprint of a large indoor plant. At 25 kg, it's light enough for one person to move and reposition. You can set it up for a workout and fold it away when you're done, making it ideal for apartments, small homes, and shared living spaces."
          }
        },
        "qa_4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's included with the Vesta Sensol App? Is there a monthly fee?",
            "answer": "The Vesta Sensol App is included free with your FLEX AIR purchase — no monthly subscription required. You get access to all 300+ guided classes, structured programmes, workout tracking, and progressive difficulty levels. This saves you up to $480 per year compared to NordicTrack ($34/month for iFIT) or Frame Fitness ($39.99/month)."
          }
        },
        "qa_5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the FLEX AIR compare to the Fortis Foldable Reformer?",
            "answer": "The Fortis ($279–$349 from Kogan) is the cheapest reformer in Australia, but it uses basic springs with no app connectivity, no guided classes, no adjustable arms, and limited warranty. The FLEX AIR offers spring-based resistance with spring resistance levels, 300+ guided classes, dual-function Pilates-plus-strength capability, Wi-Fi/Bluetooth connectivity, and a Lifetime Warranty. It's a completely different category of product."
          }
        },
        "qa_6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use the FLEX AIR for strength training, not just Pilates?",
            "answer": "Yes — that's one of the FLEX AIR's biggest advantages. The included short handles, barbell bar, and adjustable arm positions (0–132°) enable rows, chest presses, bicep curls, lateral raises, and more. Three training modes (Standard, Off-centre, Constant) further expand your strength training options. No traditional reformer on the Australian market offers this dual-function capability."
          }
        },
        "qa_7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the warranty and return policy?",
            "answer": "The FLEX AIR comes with a Lifetime Warranty on the frame and structural components, plus a 30-Day Money-Back Guarantee. If you're not completely satisfied within 30 days, return it for a full refund. Warranty claims are handled locally in Australia by Dute Fitness (Australia) Pty. Ltd. — no international shipping or long wait times."
          }
        },
        "qa_8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does shipping take? Is it really free?",
            "answer": "Shipping is completely free to all Australian addresses. Standard delivery takes 3–7 business days to metro areas (Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane, Perth, Adelaide) and 5–10 business days to regional areas. You'll receive tracking information via email once your order is dispatched."
          }
        },
        "qa_9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need any tools to assemble the FLEX AIR?",
            "answer": "Minimal assembly is required and all necessary tools are included. Most users have the FLEX AIR ready for their first workout within 15–20 minutes of unboxing. The quick-start guide provides step-by-step instructions, and the Vesta Sensol App includes a setup video tutorial."
          }
        },
        "qa_10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I upgrade from the FLEX AIR to a higher model later?",
            "answer": "While the FLEX AIR is a complete system on its own, Sensol offers a range of models with increasing resistance capacity. If you find yourself outgrowing the FLEX AIR's 120 kg max load, the FLEX PRO (150 kg max load) and FLEX PRO (150 kg max load) offer natural upgrade paths. Contact our support team at support@sensolfitness.com.au to discuss upgrade options."
          }
        }
      },
